(6258343, 925929, 115307, '<td valign="top">Seriously sick shot! I love this.<br/>It kind of stretches the boundary of what I would consider a portrait, but I am giving you the benefit of the doubt just because I love the feel of this image. The movement captured here is just awesome. 7</td>', 'Seriously sick shot! I love this.It kind of stretches the boundary of what I would consider a portrait, but I am giving you the benefit of the doubt just because I love the feel of this image. The movement captured here is just awesome. 7', '2010-12-20 15:42:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258345, 925911, 115307, '<td valign="top">Nice portrait that meets the challenge well, with some really nice lightening.<br/>I think this would have done better if there was an answer to "Why is there a girl sitting in the middle of the road?". This way it appears fairly random...like "we have a road, we have a girl, lets do this". If you had provided a story for it (by placing some other object in the photo, or whatever) I think you would have resonated with the audience more strongly and it would have scored higher for me. Technically it is very sound. 6</td>', 'Nice portrait that meets the challenge well, with some really nice lightening.I think this would have done better if there was an answer to "Why is there a girl sitting in the middle of the road?". This way it appears fairly random...like "we have a road, we have a girl, lets do this". If you had provided a story for it (by placing some other object in the photo, or whatever) I think you would have resonated with the audience more strongly and it would have scored higher for me. Technically it is very sound. 6', '2010-12-20 15:46:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258347, 925917, 115307, '<td valign="top">Great shot! I had an idea like this but never would have achieved it as well as you. This is very dramatic and well done.<br/>I think a vertical shot that cut out the christmas trees would have been even more dramatic.<br/>Awesome shot, I hope it does well for you. 7</td>', 'Great shot! I had an idea like this but never would have achieved it as well as you. This is very dramatic and well done.I think a vertical shot that cut out the christmas trees would have been even more dramatic.Awesome shot, I hope it does well for you. 7', '2010-12-20 15:48:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258348, 925868, 115307, '<td valign="top">This is awesome. I just love this and it is my top pick for this challenge. This is just 100% perfectly executed.<br/>The toast coming out of the oven is the best touch. 10</td>', 'This is awesome. I just love this and it is my top pick for this challenge. This is just 100% perfectly executed.The toast coming out of the oven is the best touch. 10', '2010-12-20 15:49:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258350, 925589, 115307, '<td valign="top">This is a little underexposed for me and could also use some more contrast. I think working with the lighting would have provided you with a much stronger shot. Very cute though, the arm reaching behind her head is a nice touch.</td>', 'This is a little underexposed for me and could also use some more contrast. I think working with the lighting would have provided you with a much stronger shot. Very cute though, the arm reaching behind her head is a nice touch.', '2010-12-20 15:51:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258352, 925834, 115307, '<td valign="top">Wow this is fantastic. So emotive and powerful.<br/>I don''t know if the general dpc audience will like this a lot too, but it certainly resonates with me.<br/>The depth of focus is just perfect here, any more would have been too much.</td>', 'Wow this is fantastic. So emotive and powerful.I don''t know if the general dpc audience will like this a lot too, but it certainly resonates with me.The depth of focus is just perfect here, any more would have been too much.', '2010-12-20 15:54:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258353, 925903, 115307, '<td valign="top">I very much love the editing here, the general tones, the textures etc. But I think it might have been composed more thoughtfully to make it stronger. The cement on the left and front of the car on the right stick out to me as examples of this. I do like this shot though 6</td>', 'I very much love the editing here, the general tones, the textures etc. But I think it might have been composed more thoughtfully to make it stronger. The cement on the left and front of the car on the right stick out to me as examples of this. I do like this shot though 6', '2010-12-20 15:57:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258379, 925840, 16148, '<td valign="top">I like your entry and hope it does well.  One thing that bothers me is the amount of detail in the windows.  It''s a beautiful piece of architecture but it dwarfs your subject.  My eye is drawn to the top window and not the young girl.  Because this is a portrait, I''d crop more off the top and maybe just leave the small windows above the door.  Either way it''s a nice shot.  Good luck!</td>', 'I like your entry and hope it does well.  One thing that bothers me is the amount of detail in the windows.  It''s a beautiful piece of architecture but it dwarfs your subject.  My eye is drawn to the top window and not the young girl.  Because this is a portrait, I''d crop more off the top and maybe just leave the small windows above the door.  Either way it''s a nice shot.  Good luck!', '2010-12-20 16:40:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258383, 925840, 104161, '<td valign="top">Wise spoken!<br/>Nice shoot!</td>', 'Wise spoken!Nice shoot!', '2010-12-20 16:56:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258385, 925874, 61084, '<td valign="top">It looks like you shot this using a cloudy, shade or even tungsten white balance setting. The color cast is very bad unfortunately. The warmth of the color cast doesn''t correlate with the coldness of the winter scene. Try using a daylight or sunny white balance to get it close or shoot in RAW to adjust the white balance in processing. Then you can remove the color cast and push the temp either way. I suggest a much cooler temp for this scene. Also, if you can adjust the exposure compensation on your camera as well as the ability to shoot in something other than auto such as aperture priority mode try setting the it to +1 EV for winter scenes to expose the snow properly. A little trial and error depending on a clear or overcast day. Good luck.</td>', 'It looks like you shot this using a cloudy, shade or even tungsten white balance setting. The color cast is very bad unfortunately. The warmth of the color cast doesn''t correlate with the coldness of the winter scene. Try using a daylight or sunny white balance to get it close or shoot in RAW to adjust the white balance in processing. Then you can remove the color cast and push the temp either way. I suggest a much cooler temp for this scene. Also, if you can adjust the exposure compensation on your camera as well as the ability to shoot in something other than auto such as aperture priority mode try setting the it to +1 EV for winter scenes to expose the snow properly. A little trial and error depending on a clear or overcast day. Good luck.', '2010-12-20 17:03:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6258386, 925914, 61084, '<td valign="top">Love this shot. Well done and very festive. :)</td>', 'Love this shot. Well done and very festive. :)', '2010-12-20 17:03:48.000000', NULL, 1),
